{"url": "https://www.jpmorgan.com/insights/global-research/commodities/silver-prices", "summary": "* **J.P. Morgan's forecast for silver prices in 2026**: According to J.P. Morgan Global Research, silver prices are expected to average **$81 per ounce** in 2026. However, the forecast also includes quarterly projections, with the **fourth quarter of 2026** averaging **$85 per ounce**, and the **annual average for 2026** at **$81 per ounce**. The report notes that silver prices rose over **130% in 2025**, driven by industrial demand and tariff uncertainty, which was partially resolved in mid-January 2026. The forecast suggests volatility, with prices dipping after the U.S. decided not to impose new tariffs on silver imports and after the nomination of Kevin Warsh as the next Fed chair, which caused a 27% crash in silver prices alongside a 10% drop in gold prices([#1](https://www.jpmorgan.com/insights/global-research/commodities/silver-prices))**. 

These projections provide a basis for evaluating whether silver will settle above **$85** on the final trading day of June 2026, but actual settlement prices will depend on market conditions at that time. The **Active Month** for CME Silver (SI) futures in June 2026 would be the nearest delivery-cycle month (March, May, July, September, December) that is not the spot month. Since June is not a delivery month, the Active Month for June would likely be **July 2026**, and the settlement price would be for the **July 2026 contract**. 

The J.P. Morgan forecast suggests that prices could be volatile, and while the fourth-quarter average is projected at **$85/oz**, this does not guarantee that the **July 2026 contract** will settle above **$85** on the final trading day of June 2026. Further market developments, including Fed policy, global demand, and tariff decisions, will influence the actual price.", "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["silver price forecast 2026 commodities outlook"], "step": 0}}

